# UI Components & Styling Guide

This project uses shadcn/ui components with Tailwind CSS v4 and Lucide React icons.

## shadcn/ui Configuration

Configuration in [components.json](mdc:components.json):

- **Style**: New York variant
- **Base Color**: Gray
- **CSS Variables**: Enabled for theming
- **Icon Library**: Lucide React
- **Aliases**: `@/components`, `@/lib/utils`, `@/components/ui`

## Component Structure

### Base UI Components

Located in `app/components/ui/`:

- [button.tsx](mdc:app/components/ui/button.tsx) - Primary button component
- [input.tsx](mdc:app/components/ui/input.tsx) - Form input component
- [alert-dialog.tsx](mdc:app/components/ui/alert-dialog.tsx) - Modal dialogs
- [sonner.tsx](mdc:app/components/ui/sonner.tsx) - Toast notifications

### Feature Components

Located in `app/components/`:

- Domain-specific components (e.g., `sqlite/` directory)
- Layout components (`NavBar.tsx`, `ThemeSwitchButton.tsx`)
- PWA components (`PWAReload.tsx`)

## Styling Patterns

### Utility Classes with `cn()`

The [app/lib/utils.ts](mdc:app/lib/utils.ts) provides `cn()` function for conditional classes:

```typescript
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'

function Button({ className, variant = 'default', ...props }) {
  return (
    <button
      className={cn(
        'base-button-classes',
        variant === 'destructive' && 'destructive-classes',
        className
      )}
      {...props}
    />
  )
}
```

### Component Variants with CVA

Use `class-variance-authority` for component variants:

```typescript
import { cva, type VariantProps } from 'class-variance-authority'

const buttonVariants = cva('base-classes', {
  variants: {
    variant: {
      default: 'default-classes',
      destructive: 'destructive-classes',
    },
    size: {
      default: 'default-size',
      sm: 'small-size',
    },
  },
  defaultVariants: {
    variant: 'default',
    size: 'default',
  },
})

type ButtonProps = VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants> &
  React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>
```

## Theming

### Dark Mode Support

- Uses `next-themes` for theme management
- Custom theme switch in [app/components/ThemeSwitchButton.tsx](mdc:app/components/ThemeSwitchButton.tsx)
- CSS variables defined in [app/index.css](mdc:app/index.css)

### Theme Hook

```typescript
import { useTheme } from '@/lib/useTheme'

function Component() {
  const { theme, setTheme, systemTheme } = useTheme()

  return (
    <button onClick={() => setTheme(theme === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark')}>
      Toggle Theme
    </button>
  )
}
```

## Icon Usage

### Lucide React Icons

```typescript
import { User, Settings, Database } from 'lucide-react'

function IconExample() {
  return (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
      <User className="h-4 w-4" />
      <Settings className="h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground" />
      <Database className="h-6 w-6 text-primary" />
    </div>
